# A Set of a small fieldless enum is stored as one U64 word: `bits()` reads
# it, `Set<E>.from_bits(n)` builds it back (None for a bit no case stands
# for), a `#Specified` enum crosses as its own single-bit values, and a
# struct holding the Set is 8 bytes. The same on every tier.
fixture: set_bits_round_trip_on_every_tier/input
step: jet run run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "3\ntrue\n2\nnone\n65\ntrue\n8\n"
step o1: jet run -O1 run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "3\ntrue\n2\nnone\n65\ntrue\n8\n"
step o2: jet run -O2 run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "3\ntrue\n2\nnone\n65\ntrue\n8\n"
